{"text": "21 March 1997 DIRECT FAX: 01703 779856\n\nGS/FL\n\nDr. LF. Gaunt\n29 Canonsfield Road\nOaklands\n\nWeloyn\nHerts AL6 OPY\n\nDear Ian,\n\n\u2018Thank you for your comments and fax relating to your meeting at the Department of Health, the\nWorking Party found the information valuable and thank you for your efforts.\n\nFrom your discussions it is clear that Professor Fairweather is interested in a number of areas\nincluding:\n\u2018Those additives prohibited for use in foods, cosmetics and toiletries. It is assumed his\ninterest lies in the U.K /EC but this may not be correct.\n2. Possible interaction of additives when combined on the product.\n\nIt would be of great help to the Working Party if we had information relating to these two areas.\n1am thus writing to propose that you review the published legislation in order to establish:\n\n1, Those additives prohibited for use in food, toiletries and cosmetics within the EC and\nbeyond, if available. Note at this stage the Working Party requires a list only, without any\n\u2018comment on the properties of any identified additive.\n\n2. The presence in the legislation of control measures that consider the potential\ninteraction/synergy of mixtures of additives in food etc.\n\n90S LLizs",
